{{Quote|Two factions that I know of used the shriek-hawk sigil&mdash;Clan Vizsla and Death Watch.|[[Aran Tal]]|<ref name="Hunters">''[[Star Wars: Hunters]]''</ref>}}
'''Shriek-hawks''', known as '''''jai'galaar''''' in [[Mando'a]],<ref name="AEYNTK" /> and also called '''raptors''',<ref name="Chapter 20 AD">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 20: The Foundling}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> were a [[species]] of giant [[Diet|predatory]] [[reptavian]]<ref name="Chapter 20" /> native to the [[planet]] [[Mandalore]]<ref name="BMF 32" /> and the "[[Armorer's planet]]."<ref name="SWECG" /> 

==History==
[[File:Raptor bird.png|thumb|250px|left|A shriek-hawk with its young]]
The [[Mandalorian]] [[Clan Vizsla]] used an image of a shriek-hawk diving for its prey as their clan emblem, a symbol that was later adopted by the [[Death Watch]] Mandalorian faction. The [[Annihilation|Mandalorian cataclysm]] had wiped out the species on Mandalore,<ref name="BMF 32">{{BuildFalconCite|32|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> and they were believed to have become extinct.<ref name="TOM">{{GermanFanCite|104|Database}}</ref> However, the species survived on the other planet. One frequently caught members of [[the Tribe]] and brought them to its nest, where it fed them to its children.<ref name="Chapter 20" />

{{Creature-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Shriek-hawks first appeared in ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'' episode "[[Chapter 20: The Foundling]]."<ref name="Chapter 20" /> Although unnamed, they were confirmed to be shriek-hawks by [[Topps]] for ''[[Star Wars: Card Trader]]''.<ref name="Topps">{{ToppsDigital|url=swcardtrader/article/0da4719a-d63c-4ab9-8e33-3c707c7b2bb4|text=Featured Creature continues! Collect A Shriek-Hawk in Week 10!}}</ref>

